<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naumăchĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυμαχία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the representation of
				a sea-fight, a mock seafight</i> (pure Lat. navale proelium).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naumachiam commisit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naumachiae spectaculum edere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Caes. 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naumachiam exhibere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ner. 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 56, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 100, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart.
				Spect. 28, 12</span></i>: voluptates naumachiae, Vopisc. Aur. 34, 6.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a place where mock
				seafights were exhibited</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">edidit et navale proelium in veteri naumachia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Dom. 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
